{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>And I appeared</b> — above this is written: \"he drove them from his land,\" and adjacent to it: \"and Elohim spoke.\" This teaches that the speech with him was not in his land but outside the city." "<b>And I appeared</b> — וארא: four times written with the patriarchs. וירא — three: two with Abraham, one with Isaac, one with Jacob." "<b>And I appeared</b> — in gematria: יצחק, as this. Come and see in the Midrash: that Isaac caused Israel to go forth from Egypt. \"And I appeared to Abraham\" — ס\"ת: אלם, that they made themselves mute and did not question His ways." "<b>As El Shaddai</b> — this refers only to Abraham and Jacob, to whom He appeared as El Shaddai. And Rashi's comment: this is what is said regarding Isaac — \"and I will establish the oath that I swore to Abraham your father,\" and it is said of it: \"as El Shaddai.\" Another interpretation: \"to Abraham, to Isaac, and to Jacob, as El Shaddai, and My name YHWH\" — meaning: with these two names I appeared to them. With the name יו\"ד ה\"א I promised them to settle them in the land securely, and with the name El Shaddai I promised them to be fruitful and multiply, for this name is upon fruitfulness and multiplication. ב' of Jacob, ק' of Isaac, מ' of Abraham — and it equals ק\"מ, and it is in א\"ת ב\"ש: שדי. Therefore He appeared to them with this name. And in ר\"ת: א' of Abraham, י' of Isaac, and י' of Jacob — totals כ\"א, as the numerical value of אהיה. Behold, the Name is in ר\"ת and ס\"ת. And this is: \"The angel of YHWH encamps around those who fear Him.\"" "<b>'</b>"], :book :exodus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:12:07.280515879Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}